    <details data-faq data-faq-id="medical-courier-license"><summary>Does Maine issue a medical cannabis courier license?</summary><p>OCP does not list a general courier registration or courier endorsement for the medical program. Legal delivery must be tied to authorized medical-program conduct by the responsible caregiver or dispensary.</p></details>
    <details data-faq data-faq-id="medical-delivery-app"><summary>Can any delivery app bring medical cannabis?</summary><p>No. Ask which registered caregiver or dispensary is responsible for the transfer. A generic app or gig driver is not proof of medical-program authority.</p></details>
    <details data-faq data-faq-id="visiting-patient-delivery"><summary>Can a visiting patient receive delivery?</summary><p>Potentially, if the patient and transaction satisfy §2423-D, current OCP visiting-patient requirements, and the provider's lawful delivery procedures. Verify directly before ordering.</p></details>
    <details data-faq data-faq-id="medical-cannabis-mail"><summary>Can cannabis be mailed to a patient?</summary><p>No. Maine medical authorization does not permit shipment through the U.S. mail or transport across state lines.</p></details>
  </section>

